1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
Your brake fluid is quietly

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:03,000
pulling water out of the air.
That's chemistry.

3
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,200
Brake fluid is hygroscopic —

4
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:09,000
it absorbs moisture through
the lines, even sealed.

5
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,200
More water means a
lower boiling point —

6
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:15,000
a spongier pedal exactly
when you need it firm.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,800
It's also how corrosion starts
inside steel brake lines —

8
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:20,000
from the inside out,
where you can't see it.

9
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,200
Fifteen seconds with a
test strip tells you which one you are.

10
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:26,000
Bring it by — we'll
check it free.
